{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I had this pressure in my chest earlier today, right in the center, and it went to my back. I was sweating but didn’t feel short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did the chest pain get worse with movement?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, especially when I moved or took a deep breath. But then, while I was getting scanned, the pain moved to my belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Where in your belly did it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Mainly on the right side and upper middle. It was sharp and worse when I breathed deeply."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ve checked your heart with an EKG and blood tests twice, and there’s no sign of a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, but I was worried because I had chest pain just a couple weeks ago too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw your records. That episode was also non-cardiac. We did a CT scan of your chest, and it ruled out a blood clot or a tear in the aorta."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s causing the belly pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re still figuring that out. We did an ultrasound and a CT scan of your abdomen, and both were mostly normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Mostly? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because of your body habitus, the ultrasound was limited. But it did show your liver is a bit fatty, which is common and not usually painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that before. But this pain is new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2144-10-28 19:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The CT scan didn’t show any gallstones, infection, or free fluid. You’ve had your gallbladder out, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, years ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also checked your blood for pancreas and liver issues. Everything looks normal except your alkaline phosphatase is a bit high, but it’s been that way before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what do you think it is?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of gastritis and the location of the pain, we think it might be stomach-related. We’re going to increase your pantoprazole to twice a day and add famotidine at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve had that before. But I’ve also been having diarrhea in the mornings for about a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I saw that. We tested for C. diff, and it was negative. Your stool didn’t show any blood either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should we do more tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Since you’re not dehydrated and the pain isn’t severe, we’ll let your primary doctor and a GI specialist look into it after you’re discharged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2144-10-28 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s better. Still tender in the upper belly, especially on the right, but not as sharp."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We repeated an X-ray of your abdomen this morning to make sure there’s no free air or blockage. It was normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing’s torn or blocked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, everything looks intact. Your labs this morning are stable too. The pain seems to be improving with the new meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. What about that scan that showed my pulmonary artery is a bit enlarged?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the chest CT did show that. It might suggest mild pulmonary hypertension, but it’s been seen before. Your primary doctor should follow up on that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2144-10-29 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll mention it at my next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. Your pain is much better, and all the tests are reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep taking the pantoprazole twice a day and add famotidine at bedtime. They’ll help reduce stomach acid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with your primary care provider within a week. They can refer you to a gastroenterologist to check for gastritis or other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another scope?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. An EGD could help see if there’s inflammation or an ulcer. Your GI doctor will decide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2144-10-29 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll set that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2144-10-29 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. Any new pain or symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2144-10-29 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling better. Just a little sore when I press on my belly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2144-10-29 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Keep an eye on it. If the pain comes back or gets worse, don’t hesitate to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2144-10-29 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2144-10-29 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and follow up as planned."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2144-10-28 19:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2144-10-29 20:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of hypertension, type 2 diabetes, hyperlipidemia, coronary artery disease, pseudotumor cerebri with a VP shunt, obstructive sleep apnea, depression, and obesity was admitted for chest pain that migrated to abdominal pain. Initial evaluation showed no evidence of acute coronary syndrome, pulmonary embolism, or aortic dissection. The chest pain resolved, but she developed right upper quadrant and epigastric pain. Imaging studies, including abdominal ultrasound and CT, were unremarkable except for fatty liver and a stable VP shunt. Pain was attributed to possible gastritis, and her pantoprazole was increased to twice daily with addition of famotidine at night. She also reported a month-long history of watery diarrhea, which was negative for C. diff and blood; outpatient GI follow-up was recommended. She improved symptomatically and was discharged home in stable condition.",
    "problems": [
      "Other chest pain",
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus without complications",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery without angina pectoris",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 40.0-44.9, adult",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence",
      "Diarrhea, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
